  "id": "fon_vodun_ceremonial",
  "name": "Vodun ceremonial music (Fon of southern Benin)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Ceremonial drumming and song of vodun worship among the Fon and neighbouring Gbe-speaking peoples of southern Benin, centred on the former Dahomey capital Abomey and the coastal town of Ouidah, where each vodun deity has its own rhythms, songs and dances performed by initiates. Ensembles of drums with an iron double bell and gourd rattles accompany call-and-response singing. The membrane-drum card stands in for the vodun drums and the agogo card for the iron bell.",
